{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792620000000-engineer-8d.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 13:30 +07\n# Task: phase 8 slice 8d, the old transport out (codex implements)\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8d`, branch `srvm-phase8d` from `srvm-phase8` (= master 67b98907). Reviewed afterwards by a NON-codex reviewer with mutants. READ FIRST: `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`; `collab/phase8-plan.md` IN FULL (sections 1.1 delete list, 1.5 the old transport paths and who exercises them, 2 Q2 and Q7, 3 slice 8d row, the coverage audit rule); continuation design `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` 8.4 (replacement coverage). OWNER RULINGS: the old codec versions 0/1/2, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc` (3783 lines), `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/checkpoint.cljc` (old inspector) and their tests DIE in this slice (no production requirer; the row carrier + `rows.checkpoint` replaced them in phase 7); no compatibility shim or version dispatch; the de Bruijn kernels stay (backends); dao.jing untouched; ALWAYS preserve coverage: before deleting a test file list every deftest in it and for each name a surviving deftest that covers it or write one (the plan's coverage audit); the suite's deftest count may drop only by tests OF DELETED CODE, documented. Do NOT touch the other orchestrator's C4 files except where the plan lists `test/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:241` and `int_contract_test.cljc:483` (they use the old transport): port those two lines to the holder path ONLY if trivial; otherwise leave them and list them in the report as blocked on the freeze (8f) and keep their test namespaces compiling by leaving the old namespaces they need until 8f? NO: decide: if deleting `handoff.cljc` breaks them, do not delete `handoff.cljc` in this slice; instead delete everything else and report precisely which two C4 tests still require it, and why (so the freeze in 8f removes them together). \nDo: (1) first move the helpers other surviving tests borrow from `lift_support.cljc`, `v2_support.cljc` and `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc` into `rows_support.cljc` (the plan lists the requirers: `frame_test`, `layout_test`, `semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test`, `holder/*`, authority tests, etc.); (2) delete `handoff.cljc` and `checkpoint.cljc` (subject to the C4 caveat above), the 15 old-codec test files, `lift_support.cljc`, `v2_support.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`, `checkpoint-v1.txt`, `handoff-v2.txt`, `scalars-v1.txt` and its minter; keep `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`, `ledger-v2.txt`; (3) add one `rows_test` row that a version-0, version-1 or version-2 header is `:yin.k/undecodable` (confirm what the codec answers; do not invent); (4) the coverage audit written into the report: for every deleted deftest, the surviving test or a new one; (5) docs: nothing now (8g). If anything the plan says disagrees with the code, the code wins: report it. Portability: `.cljc` JVM/Node/Dart rules (no `for` over long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`).\nVerification, foreground, JVM only: `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>`; every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace (quick `-e :slow` and `-i :slow` with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` for the slow ones; stage-e process test needs `npm ci` first); `yin.vm.semantic-register.*`; `rows_test`, harness and layout root ids unchanged; deftest counts before/after in the report. Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify): a helper moved to `rows_support` altered; the new version-header refusal test removed; a deleted test's behaviour broken in the surviving code. Do not commit. Report `collab/1792620000000-engineer-8d.report.md`: files deleted/changed with line counts, test counts before/after, the coverage audit, the C4 caveat resolution, mutants, deviations, design defects.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
