{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -6 /tmp/phase8d-initial.log; head -55 test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; cat test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc | head -35; sed -n '75,86p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; rg 's/' test/yang/python/antlr/int_contract_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"counterexample-search frame-bearing 40 states: {:numbered 37, :refused 3, :max-work 125296} failures: 0\ncounterexample-search with children 20 states: {:numbered 19, :refused 1, :max-work 308801} failures: 0\ncounterexample-search incidence families 100 states: {:numbered 74, :refused 26, :max-work 421748} failures: 0\n\nRan 76 tests containing 4298 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test\n  \"Phase 7a: custody on rows (phase-7 plan §3.1). The lift under a header\n   writes the root's custody slot by kind and refuses :op-seq-exhausted,\n   :unprotected-pending and an id on an unenrolled stream; the lower's\n   custody stage runs the custody grammar, refuses a fork under\n   :exclusive, runs the version-1 grant checks on a blocked or parked\n   exclusive root, protection in both directions and op-id presence equal\n   to enrollment, restores the counter exactly, lowers a halted exclusive\n   root with no grant gated :ended, and every refusal comes before the\n   first attach (zero attachments). The version-1 rules these re-pin are\n   lift_v1_test's and handoff_v2_custody_test's, kept until phase 8.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-fixtures :as f]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n\n\n(defn- custody-of\n  [wire]\n  (nth (:slots (rows/decode wire)) 16))\n\n\n(defn- identities\n  \"Every stream identity of the pack's tree.\"\n  [wire]\n  (into #{} (keep (fn [r] (when (= :stream (second r)) (nth r 2)))) (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The lift under a header\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest the-lift-writes-the-custody-slot-by-kind\n                       (vec (mapcat identity (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\n                       (vec slots))})\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  [status kind path]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Row codec refused data\"\n                  {:yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path path})))\n\n\n(defn- bad!\n  [kind path]\n   test/resources/yang/python/int-contract-v1.txt hold on this host.\n          m (vm/run (s/load-ast (s/new-machine {:modules wide})\n                                (s/app (s/v 'integer/pow) (s/lit 2)\n                                       (s/lit 100))))\n          r (s/lift m nil)\n          out (rows/lower-task (s/new-machine {:modules small}) r (fn [_] nil))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
