{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > /tmp/phase8d-report.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,re,subprocess\nbefore=json.loads(Path('/tmp/phase8d-before.json').read_text())\naudit=json.loads(Path('/tmp/phase8d-audit.json').read_text())\ndef names(s):return re.findall(r'\\\\(deftest\\\\s+(?:\\\\\"'^:slow'\"\\\\s+)?([\"'^'\"\\\\s()]+)',s)\ncount=sum(len(names(p.read_text())) for p in Path('test').rglob('*') if p.suffix in ['.clj','.cljc','.cljs','.cljd'])\nassert count==before['tests']-141+3,(before['tests'],count)\nchanged=subprocess.check_output(['git','diff','--name-only'],text=True).splitlines()\nbase='''Created-Local: 2026-10-14 +07\n# Phase 8d engineer report\n\nImplemented the legacy-test/support cutover. No commit. **Physical removal of the two legacy production files is deferred to 8f under the prompt's C4 caveat.** All 15 legacy test files (141 deftests), three support files, three fixtures and scalar minter are removed. Surviving tests own their helpers in \"'`rows_support.cljc`; there is no compatibility namespace or added version dispatch.\n\n## C4 caveat and retained files\n\n- `yang.python.antlr.int-heap-test/cell-refusal-test`, through private `cell-refusal`, still calls `handoff/export-task` at line 241. Its `run-all` covers the AST walker, old v3 semantic kernel, de Bruijn stack and register. A one-line substitution cannot lift those machines as canonical row tasks: the row lift accepts semantic-register state; the native backends require their layout conversion, and the walker/old semantic setup must change. That would edit this C4 file'\"'s kernel harness beyond the permitted trivial port. The file is untouched; its targeted slow test passes (1 test, 24 assertions). This is the remaining freeze/8f blocker.\n- \"'`yang.python.antlr.int-contract-test/an-image-carries-no-profile-test` was trivial to port. The single halted numeric result now uses a semantic-register machine, a fork row pack and `rows/lower-task` (the carrier APIs the holder uses). Its integer composition, no-carried-limits assertion and wide/small results remain checked. This exercises the carrier directly, rather than constructing an authority/holder lifecycle for an already halted result. No other C4 file changed.\n- Retain `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc` unchanged (3783 lines). Retain `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/checkpoint.cljc` unchanged (541 lines), because handoff requires that inspector. Deleting the latter alone would break the allowed retained namespace. Remove both with the remaining heap test'\"'s port during the freeze in 8f. There are no production requirers outside this retained pair.\n- Both C4 namespaces compile. The integer-contract quick namespace passed with rows tests; the retained heap slow test was executed explicitly.\n\n## Changes and line counts\n\nCounts below are complete file lines at HEAD versus the final worktree, not diff hunk lengths.\n\n| File | Before | After | Action |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n'''\nfor file in changed:\n old=subprocess.check_output(['git','show','HEAD:'+file],text=True)\n p=Path(file)\n base+=f'| \"'`{file}` | {len(old.splitlines())} | {len(p.read_text().splitlines()) if p.exists() else 0} | {\"changed\" if p.exists() else \"deleted\"} |'\"\\\\n'\nbase+='''\n\"'`rows_support` owns the AST constructors, deterministic one-slot stream and serve table, custody constants/header/op-id helpers, public ring, remote toy/peer/server/mirror/attacher and call-node/stream-of helpers. Only borrowed live helpers moved; obsolete old-kernel builders and version-aware codec drivers were removed. The existing local counting `attacher` stays distinct from `remote-attacher`, which connects the toy channel. Frame/layout/harness, composition and fencing requirers now use rows support, with no duplicate requires. `checkpoint_fixtures` had no surviving borrower; its row successor was already independent.\n\nNew `rows-test` deftests:\n\n1. `legacy-version-headers-refuse-before-attachment`: 0, 1 and 2 headers refuse with the exact observed `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, kind `:version`, path `[:yin.k/version]`, with zero attachments.\n2. `numeric-scalars-round-trip-through-rows`: all integer-contract boundary values, explicitly typed floats (positive/negative zero, NaN, infinity, subnormal, 2''^53, 2''^63), strings/Unicode, booleans and nil; tests both numeric literals in carried code and values in halted results; canonical CBOR equality and existing integer CBOR goldens.\n3. `result-only-values-complete-the-census`: repeated versus independent result-only cursors retain their topology and exact census/attach counts; result-only plain/module closures bring their code and module cursor stores. Adds the corresponding row helper for a halted module closure.\n\n## Test counts and scope\n\n'\"'''\nbase+=f'Actual textual deftest inventory over \"'`test/**/*.(clj|cljc|cljs|cljd)`: **{before[\"tests\"]} before, {count} after = {before[\"tests\"]} − 141 + 3**. The plan'\"\\\\'s 4574 is stale at this branch. Counts use \"'`'\"\\\\\\\\(deftest\\\\\\\\s+(?:\\\\\\\\\"'^:slow'\"\\\\\\\\s+)?([\"'^'\"\\\\\\\\s()]+)\"'`, the same extraction before/after. This is a source count; JVM runner totals differ because of host conditions and metadata filters. No surviving deftest was removed. The 141 reduction is exactly the 15 retired old-transport files listed below; physical implementation deletion awaits the authorized C4 exception.'\"\\\\n\\\\n'\nbase+='''## Verification\n\nForeground JVM commands (logs retained under \"'`target/phase8d/`):\n\n- `npm ci`: passed (69 packages); required before Stage E'\"'s JVM runner builds/spawns its Node peer.\n- \"'`clj -M:kondo --lint <8 modified .cljc files>`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `clj -M:test -e :slow -r '\"'\"'^yin'\"\\\\\\\\.vm\\\\\\\\.(ucf\\\\\\\\.|semantic-register\\\\\\\\.).*-test\"'$'\"'\"'`: passed, 754 tests / 19205 assertions, 0 failures/errors. This sweep included the first two new tests; the final third new test and extended scalar code cases are covered by the final focused run below. Every surviving test namespace under both prefixes was selected. The process namespace has only slow deftests.\n- `clj -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-contract-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test`: passed on final code, 47 tests / 1386 assertions, 0 failures/errors.\n- After restoring mutants, the three new row tests plus `rows-checkpoint-test/the-file-holds-exactly-the-declared-bytes`: 4 tests / 54 assertions, 0 failures/errors.\n- `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 clj -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.int-heap-test -v yang.python.antlr.int-heap-test/cell-refusal-test`: passed, 1 test / 24 assertions.\n- `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 clj -M:test -i :slow -r '\"'\"'^yin'\"\\\\\\\\.vm\\\\\\\\.(ucf\\\\\\\\.|semantic-register\\\\\\\\.).*-test\"'$'\"'\"'`: **PENDING_SLOW**.\n- `git diff --check`: clean. Address literals in `rows_test`, layout and harness are byte-for-byte unchanged against HEAD; all their existing root assertions passed. `git diff --quiet` confirms `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`, `ledger-v2.txt`, corpus and all production source files are unchanged. No hashes were reminted.\n\nThe prompt explicitly requests JVM only; a Node peer exercised by the JVM Stage E process harness is part of that required gate. No standalone Node/Dart test lane or tri-host landing claim is made.\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutation used `cp` to back up the current worktree file, a saved diff, a foreground check, `cp` to restore, and a quiet diff against the backup. Production restoration also passed `git diff --quiet -- src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc`.\n\n| Mutant | Check | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Moved one-slot stream'\"'s initial cursor 0 → 1 in \"'`rows_support` | `rows-checkpoint-test/the-file-holds-exactly-the-declared-bytes` | Killed: 1 test / 1 assertion, 1 failure, pinned checkpoint bytes changed. |\n| Remove `legacy-version-headers-refuse-before-attachment` entirely | Required-deftest audit (`assert '\"'(deftest legacy-version-headers-refuse-before-attachment' in rows_test\"'`) | Killed by audit: assertion `required phase-8d refusal test missing`. This is an audit/count check, not a behavioral test failure. Existing `gates-and-graph-before-hashes` overlaps header refusal coverage; removing a redundant deftest need not fail the runtime suite. |\n| Corrupt restored `:value` to `:mutant` in `rows/lower-task` | `rows-test/numeric-scalars-round-trip-through-rows`, successor of deleted scalar-round-trip behavior | Killed: 1 test / 35 assertions, 2 failures (code-literal and result-only paths). |\n\nAn initial helper mutant invocation used `-v` without `-n`; the runner'\"'s default discovery tried unrelated ANTLR tests and failed because Python3Lexer was not generated in this worktree. That attempt is not counted as a kill. It was restored and rerun with the precise namespace above. The first prefix-regex invocation also selected 0 tests (the runner matches the whole namespace); the corrected regex above selected the actual sweep. Both command-selection corrections are recorded rather than treated as verification.\n\n## Deviations and design defects\n\n1. **Header refusal status discrepancy:** the brief/plan says \"'`:yin.k/undecodable`. Actual `rows/decode*` explicitly raises `:yin.k/profile-mismatch :version` before row/hash checks; existing `gates-and-graph-before-hashes` already expects it. The new test pins the code'\"'s actual answer without altering the codec or inventing dispatch. This is a plan/acceptance-description defect, not a newly introduced production defect.\n2. **C4 exception needs both production namespaces retained:** handoff requires checkpoint. No shim was created and no old codec version was added to the holder. The old direct test suites are retired as explicitly requested; the remaining direct C4 test accounts for physical retention until 8f.\n3. The profile test ports directly to the row carrier underlying the holder rather than adding an authority lifecycle to a halted result; the no-profile payload contract is preserved.\n4. Added two coverage tests beyond the requested header row because scalar code/value classes and result-only dependency/cursor census need explicit replacement evidence.\n5. Legacy wire-specific acceptance, dispatch, mixed engine profiles, old per-engine register/walker frame syntax, old fixture bytes and v0 big-content refusal are retired facts. The audit names the surviving row contracts, not a claim that obsolete wire formats remain accepted. Rows have a single canonical profile; backends carry/restore through layout. Row restrictions (for example blocked install children only, reserved guest marker refusal, absence of an explicit native layout list) replace those old shapes. No attempt widens the retained backend fragment or revives legacy dispatch.\n6. No design documentation changed (8g). No production behavioral changes or newly discovered production defects beyond the described acceptance-status discrepancy.\n\n## Coverage audit: all 141 deleted deftests\n\nThe names were extracted and mapped before file deletion; each named surviving target was checked to exist. The two supplemental tests close result-only and numeric code/value gaps identified during the audit. The table maps enduring behavior to a surviving row/kernel contract. For legacy-only formats, the successor test documents the new boundary; old bytes, supported-version sets, per-engine dispatch and native frame representation assertions die with the retired suite. Source test count is not used as a substitute for this mapping.\n\nAbbreviations (each cell is \"'`namespace-alias/deftest`):\n\n- H = `yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test`\n- R = `yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`\n- C = `yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test`\n- F = `yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test`\n- G = `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test`\n- L = `yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test`\n- Other namespaces are printed in full.\n\n'\"'''\naliases={'yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test':'H','yin.vm.ucf.rows-test':'R','yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test':'C','yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test':'F','yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test':'G','yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test':'L'}\nfor file in dict.fromkeys(e[0] for e in audit):\n entries=[e for e in audit if e[0]==file]\n base+=f'### \"'`{file}` ({len(entries)} deftests)'\"\\\\n\\\\n| Deleted deftest | Surviving deftest |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n'\n for _,n,r in entries:\n  ns,name=r.rsplit('/',1);base+=f'| \"'`{n}` | `{aliases.get(ns,ns)}/{name}` |'\"\\\\n'\n base+='\\\\n'\nPath('collab/1792620000000-engineer-8d.report.md').write_text(base)\nprint('count:',count,'report lines:',len(base.splitlines()))\nPY\npython3 /tmp/phase8d-report.py\nmkdir -p target/phase8d\ncp /tmp/phase8d-*.log /tmp/phase8d-mutant-*.diff /tmp/phase8d-audit.json /tmp/phase8d-inventory.json target/phase8d/\nclj -M:kondo --lint \"'$(cat /tmp/phase8d-changed.txt) > /tmp/phase8d-lint.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
